    "name": "rolling-hours-max-the-averaging-multiplies-both-the-window-and-the-cap",
    "why": "THE PLAN'S OWN 100/100/60/60 CASE, SCALED. Two conditions over one world, and they disagree by a multiplication nobody performs while looking at a gate screen. p-ali holds four twelve-hour duties in two adjacent pairs: 48 h. The averaged rule (12 h in 2 days, averaged over 4 windows) is 48 h in any 8 consecutive days and is clean at exactly the limit; the unaveraged rule with the same 12 h figure is breached twice, once per pair. A reading of averaging as \"the mean of the windows\" or as \"each window separately\" gives a different answer here, which is the whole reason the preview prints both scales.",
